## build order

build in phases. each phase delivers something testable. don't move to next phase until current one works end-to-end.

### phase 1 — foundation

- next.js repo setup, typescript
- copy existing reader code into `/app/page.tsx`, strip english column
- keep all existing styling untouched
- script toggle (placeholder UI only)
- create `data/book_4.json` seeded with first 10 couplets (harkirat will provide farsi + his manual punjabi translations as initial seed/style examples)
- `/about` page (placeholder, harkirat fills in content later)

### phase 2 — workbench shell

- middleware password gate on `/admin`
- `/admin` page with batch view: render couplet cards from `data/book_4.json`
- batch size selector, jump-to-couplet, position indicator (all functional)
- approve button: just toggles status="approved" in the local json, no AI yet
- no AI calls in this phase — verify ui/data flow works first

### phase 3 — AI integration

- create `system_prompt.md` (initial version: translation philosophy + script rules + vocabulary preferences)
- `lib/claude.ts` with the three call functions
- wire up: untranslated couplets auto-draft on batch load
- wire up: word click → popover with alternatives
- wire up: regenerate button
- logging plumbing (`data/logs/book_4.jsonl`)

### phase 4 — publishing

- implement "approve batch & push to reader" → writes to `public/book_4.json`
- deploy reader to github pages
- workbench stays local-only (never deployed publicly)

### phase 5 — translate book 4

- not a build phase, a usage phase
- harkirat works through ~3,800 couplets in batches
- `system_prompt.md` updated by harkirat directly when patterns emerge

